# 13. MODULE SPECIFICATION: EKAM BOOKS

## Purpose

Create an affordable, trustworthy second-hand book exchange marketplace.

## Main workflow

1. User creates a book listing.
2. User adds title, author, ISBN, edition, condition, photographs, and location.
3. Backend validates listing data.
4. Other users search for books.
5. Interested user requests a book.
6. Owner accepts or rejects the request.
7. Book and any relevant credits are reserved.
8. Parties arrange shipping or local handover.
9. Recipient confirms receipt.
10. Exchange is settled.
11. Eligible reviews are submitted.

## Essential MVP screens

- Books home.
- Search.
- Search filters.
- Book details.
- Create listing.
- Edit listing.
- My listings.
- Wishlist.
- Exchange request.
- Request status.
- Handover or delivery details.
- Receipt confirmation.
- Credit history.
- Report or dispute.

## Listing fields

- Title.
- Author.
- ISBN where available.
- Edition.
- Category.
- Condition.
- Description.
- Photographs.
- Location.
- Availability.
- Credit value or exchange terms.

## Credit-ledger integrity

Implement credits as an auditable accounting mechanism.

- Never trust a client-supplied balance.
- Record every credit movement.
- Make settlement atomic.
- Prevent duplicate settlement.
- Reserve and release credits through explicit transaction states.
- Reconcile balances against ledger entries.
- Require audit records for administrative adjustments.
- Prevent the same book from being reserved for conflicting exchanges.
- Define the dispute process.

Keep paid, transferable, or cash-redeemable credits out of the initial MVP until their legal and financial implications have been assessed.

## Monetisation

Evaluate shipping services, premium listings, institutional subscriptions, and transparent service fees.

